module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_applied_generic_formal_is_called_unbound_through_the_declarations_own_parameter

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// Orientation only. Every status, count, obligation and dissolution condition this row depends on
// is a typed `receipts` entry, not a comment (gunbc.design_argument::source_annotations: "an
// invariant, receipt, event, ruling, citation, status, count or dissolution condition belongs in a
// typed carrier"), so nothing here may be deleted without losing a claim that is already carried in
// data. The class in one line: an applied generic formal reads as unbound because the shared
// predicate descends a resolved call into the container declaration's OWN parameter, so the call
// site's actual is never compared with the declared formal -- see the receipts for the measured
// chain, the population cost of the global change, and the seam-local repair that refuses it.

// Provenance (context, not correctness): filed 2026-11-26 by session eager-heron-455 from the
// executed runs under ~/scratch/eager-heron-455/stages3 on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd, aarch64), for the
// lane compiler-guarantee, work item node://list-append-refuses-an-element-argument; the rule and
// its execution receipt are in https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16894 (head
// 95304b7f00c9e3ff2ef38fb5e5bcbffb6697d3ac; the first filing named
// 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16, superseded within the same branch), this row is filed by
// https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/17161. Quoted log lines were machine-extracted with
// `grep -F`; no verdict line is retyped.

data an_applied_generic_formal_is_called_unbound_through_the_declarations_own_parameter: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_applied_generic_formal_is_called_unbound_through_the_declarations_own_parameter" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "every direct-call argument position whose declared formal is an APPLIED generic is judged against what the argument actually produced, and the walk that descends a resolved node into the type alias' own parameters is not consulted for that position; the refusal is located at the argument and names the parameter; and each shape (refusal, same-container control, element control) is carried by a data-string subject that is ALSO compiled standalone with its own exit status printed, so a wall that stops firing shows up as red at the census rather than as a passing row. EXECUTABLE PER LEG TODAY, ON AN ENROLLED ADDRESS: each leg has its own instrument target row in #gunbc.instrument_targets bound through `CliWireProgramProducer`, so the command a reader runs is `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:<target>` and the exit IS the leg's own verdict -- `list-append-wall-element-at-list-position` (leg an_element_cannot_take_a_lists_place_at_a_free_monoid_position), `list-append-wall-refusal-names-parameter` (the_refusal_names_the_parameter_and_the_reason), `list-append-wall-list-still-admitted` (a_list_still_takes_that_position), `list-append-wall-element-at-element-position` (an_element_at_a_position_declared_as_the_element_is_still_admitted), `list-append-wall-three-arms-observable` (all_three_arms_are_observable_censuses), `list-append-wall-arms-differ-by-target-row` (the_two_arms_differ_by_exactly_the_target_row), `list-append-wall-all-legs` (the module's eight folded, the two depth legs included), `list-append-wall-deep-unbound-element` (a_deep_unbound_element_below_the_removed_ceiling_is_still_judged), `list-append-wall-deep-resolved-element` (a_deep_fully_resolved_element_tree_is_still_admitted), `free-monoid-carrier-text-at-string-run-refused` (text_actual_at_run_of_string_is_refused_naming_the_right_parameter), `free-monoid-carrier-two-runs-admitted` (the_same_call_over_two_runs_is_not_refused), `free-monoid-carrier-list-push-admitted` (list_push_takes_an_element_where_an_element_is_required), `free-monoid-carrier-all-legs` (the carrier's seventeen folded), `list-append-wall-fold-cannot-absorb-a-two` (fold_cannot_absorb_a_two_wire: one member that HELD folded with one member the renderer refused). The same legs remain runnable by name with the run verb for a reading outside the registry: `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/list_append_element_argument_wall.dag --function <leg>`, and the same verb with --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag. Expected exit codes, stated so a green needs no interpretation: 0 for every leg at the wall head; at a tree without the wall 1 (a finding) for the discriminating labels list-append-wall-element-at-list-position, list-append-wall-refusal-names-parameter, list-append-wall-arms-differ-by-target-row and free-monoid-carrier-text-at-string-run-refused, and still 0 for the controls list-append-wall-list-still-admitted, list-append-wall-element-at-element-position, list-append-wall-three-arms-observable, free-monoid-carrier-two-runs-admitted and free-monoid-carrier-list-push-admitted; `list-append-wall-fold-cannot-absorb-a-two` is expected 2 on BOTH trees -- with the wall and without it -- because what it tests is the fold and not the compiler, and a 1 there means a could-not-run member was absorbed into a finding, which is the absorbing answer gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed forbids; a leg returning 2 elsewhere is the door refusing to run and is reported as could-not-run, never folded into green"
    }
  },

  receipts: [
    "**INVALID STATE: `list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\")` at `std.algebra`'s `list_append(left: FreeMonoid<T>, right: FreeMonoid<T>)` is ACCEPTED and evaluates to `[\"a\", \"bc\"]` — a `String` reaches a `FreeMonoid<T>` parameter unchecked, at a position whose declared type the compiler has already substituted to `FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>` (measured 2026-11-23 at main 97d114837edf, and again at origin/main 4cb919e4a109: the repro compiles and runs; the same acceptance re-measured under main's RELEASED parser at the s46 control legs). This is below the ordinary floor (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: values inhabit declared types), and it hides the `list_push`/`list_append` mix-up authors make.**",
    "THE PREDICATE IS NOT WRONG, ITS POSITION IS. `direct_call_formal_has_unbound_type_variable` (src/v1/04_infer.dag:7910 with its recursion `_at` at :7914 on origin/main d20fa377f6c) answers whether a type tree contains an unsolved variable, and it ORs three reads at every node: the node's own inferred (via `child_type_node`), its children, and its params (via `param_node_type_expr`). Its `Resolved` arm descends into the resolution. For a nominal application that is the wrong bookkeeping: the resolution of `FreeMonoid<T>` under a `String` argument expands the alias `FreeMonoid → Empty | Cons`, and `Cons`'s cell is `Product`'s own parameter, spelled `T`. The terminal node the walk lands on has `name=\"T\"`, `kind=type_variable`, and an EMPTY inferred — it is the declaration's parameter, not the call's element. The fact the call needs lives one level ABOVE that descent, in the settled resolution the same walk had already visited and left.",
    "MEASURED, one repro, level by level, AND THE CITATION IN THE FIRST FILING WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED HERE: it attributed this to `S38E_*` lines in `logs41b_runner.out`, and that file does not exist (S69_LOGS41B_EXISTS=NO, log stages3/logs69_counts.out; `logs41_runner.out` does exist, 52 lines). The probe output is real and lives in `stages3/s38e_term.log` and `stages3/s38e_slot.log` on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd, aarch64, tree 682a78edcfcde521a14681dba4d5d56e8d82b8f0, `S38E_TREE_SHA=` in s38e_slot.log). The census, one command per count with its own exit status, in stages3/logs69_counts.out: S69_TERM_LINES=28076 RC=0 terminal witness lines, S69_TERM_KIND_TYPEVAR=28076 RC=0 of them `term_kind=type_variable` -- every single one -- S69_LV4_LINES=382 RC=0 traces reaching depth LV4, S69_HERE_TV_TRUE_LINES=544 RC=0 lines carrying `here_tv=true`. One whole witness line, verbatim, is the descent this class is about: EHPROBEE|term|file=dag/std/algebra.dag|pos=5817|param=xs|declared=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|actual=Primitive(xs)|term_depth=4|term_kind=type_variable|term_name=\"T\"|trace=LV0|kind=resolved|shape=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|here_tv=false|n_children=1|children=[Primitive():other#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV1|kind=resolved|shape=Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>)|here_tv=false|n_children=1|children=[Primitive():other#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV2|kind=absent|shape=Coproduct(FreeMonoid)|here_tv=false|n_children=2|children=[Primitive(Empty):absent#false ; Product(Cons):absent#true]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV3|kind=absent|shape=Product(Cons)|here_tv=false|n_children=2|children=[Primitive(T):type_variable#true ; Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive()>):absent#false]|n_params=0|params=[] >> LV4|kind=type_variable|shape=Primitive(T)|here_tv=true|n_children=0|children=[]|n_params=0|params=[] -- the terminal is the declaration's OWN `T`, reached by descending a resolved node into the container it resolves to, which is why the call site cannot see it. WITHDRAWN: the first filing said \"418 of 544 sampled terminals were reached THROUGH_ALIAS_EXPANSION\"; that token appears S69_THROUGH_ALIAS_EXPANSION=0 RC=1  <-- the row claimed 418 of 544 sampled; rc=1 means the token is absent in the log (rc 1 -- absent), and 544 is the `here_tv=true` count, not a sample, so the alias-expansion share is UNMEASURED and the mechanism claim in the header rests on the code at src/v1/04_infer.dag:7910/:7914, not on that number. THE TWO-LISTS CONTROL TRACES THE SAME PATH: `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])` and `list_push([\"a\"], \"b\")` walk an identical chain, which is why no element-side rule can tell the repro from its own controls and why the repair had to be a claim about the position, not about the argument.",
    "FIRST MEASURED NEGATIVE, so nobody re-spends a stage on it: THE PARAM-SPELLING REPAIR IS MEASURED FALSE. The hypothesis was that the params arm reads the declaration's SPELLING (`param_node_type_expr`) where it should read the param's own inferred at leaf positions — the discipline `generic_actual_position_type` already records for the mirror-image read (its comment block is src/v1/04_env.dag:2282-2291, its declaration :2315, on origin/main d20fa377f6c). Instrument: every direct-call argument position in a named 10-module population, printing each param's spelling shape and its own inferred shape side by side. Result `S38D_PARAM_SPELLING_FLIPPED=0` over 27 403 sites with `S38D_PARAM_LEAF_SITES=27403`: ZERO params had a spelling that renders `T` while its own inferred renders the settled element. The repair was withdrawn by the lane manager on that measurement, not on argument.",
    "SECOND MEASURED NEGATIVE, same discipline: THE GLOBAL PREDICATE CHANGE. Removing the `Resolved` descent for application nodes inside the SHARED `_at` (the s39 mode3 candidate) is not a repair, it is a compiler-wide opinion. THE CITATION HERE IN THE FIRST FILING WAS WRONG AND IS CORRECTED: it attributed the figures to `S43_MEASURED_SEAM` / `S43_MEASURED_RED`, but those two lines in stages3/logs43_runner.out read S43_MEASURED_SEAM|sites_printed=0|REAL_TRUE_TOTAL=0|SCOPED_TRUE_TOTAL=0|KEPT=0|FLIPPED=0|FALSE_TO_TRUE=0|method=printed_from_S41SITE_lines and S43_MEASURED_RED|visits_printed=0|shared_true=0|scoped_true=0|flipped=0|method=printed_from_S41RED_lines -- the in-run extractor globbed `$D/census/C-*.err.keep`, which matched nothing (S63_INRUN_GLOB_MATCHES_NOTHING_RC=2), so it printed zeros; the census itself built clean (S43_BUILD_CENSUS_RC=0) and wrote 535 800 `S41SITE|` records into s43/census/C1.err..C10.err, which is what the LATER OFFLINE RECOMPUTES read. Measured now, each command's own exit status printed beside it: S66_LINES|err=535800 candidate records grepped (S66_RC_GREP|err=0), S66_UNIQUE|err=41463 distinct (file, position, parameter) sites (S66_RC_SORT|err=0), and S66_MEASURED|err|sites_unique=41463|shared_true=3490|scoped_true=160|kept=160|flipped=3330|false_to_true=0|basis=first_line_per_file_pos_param on the shard copies, with the two bases identical (S66_DIFF_BETWEEN_BASES=0 distinct-basename-lines-not-shared). Tie-break sensitivity measured, not assumed: S68_CONFLICT_TEST|unique=41463|keys_with_conflicting_records=10|of_those_shared_true_first=2|shared_true_first=3490|kept_first=160|flipped_first=3330, and with the opposite tie-break S68_TIEBREAK_LAST|unique=41463|shared_true=3492|kept=160|flipped=3332 (logs stages3/logs66_runner.out, stages3/logs68_runner.out). So the global change moves about 3 330 of 41 463 direct-call argument positions from true to FALSE and creates no refusal that was not already there (false_to_true=0). WITHDRAWN: the first filing said shared-true 3 498 and FLIPPED 3 338. Neither number appears in any log under stages3/ -- the same grep that located the zero lines above returns nothing for `FLIPPED=3338` and for `3498` -- and neither tie-break reaches them, so I cannot name their source and do not restate them. What IS reproduced exactly, on the dedup basis (recomputed from the committed census, S67_RC_AWK_DEDUP=0, over the tree at f5fb5230631d040c8d39c075ebb35676ca609e26 with S67_GUNBC_SHA256=f2f660c147cb42f610da3911cdfefb7ce7b9c3d8460ef3b6ab2c06c651c59ea0): S67_FLIPFILE_TOP_DEDUP=F|847|file=src/v2/std/compilers/target_model.dag F|393|file=src/v2/compiler/body_lowering_fold.dag F|231|file=src/v2/compiler/infer.dag F|218|file=src/v2/compiler/parse.dag F|115|file=src/v2/compiler/target_serialize.dag F|110|file=src/v2/std/grammar.dag , and per parameter S67_FLIPPARAM_TOP_DEDUP=P|1500|param=xs P|685|param=o P|261|param=left P|261|param=right P|229|param=value P|112|param=m . and that shared recursion has NINE consumers, each a named declaration in src/v1/04_infer.dag on origin/main d20fa377f6c: `optional_produced_at_required_declared` :5737, `direct_call_structured_application_mismatch_diags` :7643, `direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags` :7801, `one_sided_non_arrow_side_is_open` :8183 and :8184, `direct_call_arg_type_mismatch` :8266, `infer_record_lit_structural` :14430 and :14443, `parameter_default_emissions` :17282 gating record-literal mismatch, structured-application mismatch, field-cardinality diagnostics and a generic-parameter branch. Turning those sites false can SILENCE refusals in eight consumers that have nothing to do with list element demands. Refused.",
    "THE REPAIR, AND WHY THIS SHAPE: a predicate OWNED BY THE SEAM — `element_demand_direct_call_argument_formal_is_unbound` (src/v1/04_infer.dag:8138 with its recursion `_at` at :8142 on the PR head 7d51f42cf8b (the predicate itself is unchanged since 95304b7f00c, where it was first measured), inserted after the shared `_at`, and substituted at the single consumer :7991 inside `direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags`; mirror src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs) — is substituted at ONE consumer, the direct-call argument inhabitation seam's declared-side selector. It is the shared recursion with exactly one rule changed: a node that IS an application (children non-empty) does not descend its own `Resolved` arm, because its own node is its type; a bare leaf still follows its resolution. `here`, `children` and `params` keep walking, which is why genuinely-unbound carriers survive it. The shared predicate stays byte-identical, so the other eight consumers keep today's semantics BY CONSTRUCTION.",
    "PROOF THAT THE SEAM-LOCAL RULE IS A STRICT SUBSET, not a widening. Same census, same discipline about which log says what: the in-run `S43_MEASURED_RED` line is all zeros (quoted in the previous receipt), so the red-side numbers come from the offline recompute stages3/logs63_runner.out, each count with its own exit status: S63_RED_LINES=214 `S41RED|` records, and S63_MEASURED_RED|visits_printed=214|shared_true=77|scoped_true=77|flipped=0|basis=every_printed_S41RED_line -- on every printed red line the shared read and my scoped read agree, and my read refuses none of them that the shared read does not. On the unique-site basis the same log gives S63_MEASURED_SEAM_UNIQUE|sites_unique=41463|shared_true=3490|scoped_true=160|kept=160|flipped=3330|false_to_true=0|basis=first_line_per_file_pos_param: kept 160, flipped 3 330, false_to_true=0 -- the scoped read never claims a formal is unbound where the shared read does not, so it cannot hand the declared side anywhere the basis used to win. The 160 kept shapes, grouped (stages3/logs68_runner.out, S68_RC_AWK_KEPT=0): S68_KEPT_DECLARED_TOP=D|50|declared=Primitive(T) D|40|declared=Map(...) D|15|declared=Container(List,Primitive()) D|13|declared=Primitive(K) D|9|declared=Container(List,Primitive(T)) D|5|declared=Primitive(A) D|5|declared=Primitive(V) D|4|declared=Node(Outcome<Coproduct(FreeMonoid)>) , spanning S68_KEPT_DISTINCT_DECLARED=19 distinct declared shapes and summing to the 160 kept sites exactly (S68_KEPT_TOTAL_CHECK=160); the rest is a tail of 15 shapes, the largest 9. WITHDRAWN: the first filing's \"of 5 visits to the repro's argument position, 1 shared-true stayed scoped-true and 0 flipped\" is not in any log and is replaced by the measured red census above.",
    "THE WALL, AS EXECUTED: `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 'right' [RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement: a Text value is passed at a Run-of-non-Char element demand: the element is not Char and Text is not a Run carrier]: declared 'Node(FreeMonoid<Primitive(String)>)', produced 'Primitive(String)'` at a located `file:line:col` (dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag:14:69 -- a module the stage-46 runner wrote at run time and deleted at its own `trap cleanup EXIT`; no such file is committed, which the CARRIER OBLIGATION receipt below measures -- and a position with no symbol beside it by necessity: the subject is a data string compiled at run time, not a declaration). The rendering quoted is that earlier head's; the head this row cites renders the same refusal as the census subject the leg table below quotes, whose reason token is `RefusedTextAtRunOfNonCharElement` and whose parameter is `right`. It took TWO arms to fire, and that is the class's second lesson: the element demand must be armed by a `Run`-shaped declared element (`run_element_demand`) as well as by the carrier, because `FreeMonoid<T>`'s element is `T` — neither the carrier nor the element alone distinguishes the repro from `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])`.",
    "OBSERVATION THAT MADE IT MEASURABLE, AND THE LIMIT OF THE CARRIER THAT MAKES IT MEASURABLE. A subject whose call the compiler now REFUSES cannot be carried by a `test fn` claim module, because the module fails to fold before any claim runs: the fold, not the claim, is where the refusal lands, so a `test fn` fixture for the repro reports a broken module rather than a located argument-type refusal. That is why the three positional shapes are carried as data strings -- `list_append([\"a\"], \"bc\")` refused, `list_append([\"a\"], [\"b\"])` and `list_push([\"a\"], \"b\")` accepted -- and why their refusal proof is carried by a module that compiles: dag/gunbc/instruments/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag, `wall_rows_at_parameter` over `blocking_class_census`, whose 17 legs are green by execution AS INSTRUMENT LEGS on the run route at head 95304b7f00c9e3ff2ef38fb5e5bcbffb6697d3ac (run link <PLACEHOLDER-RUN-LINK>; the same legs' earlier claim-route reading at 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16, run link https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/16894#issuecomment-7201169375, is SUPERSEDED here -- the receipt below states why that route cannot read this class). The weakness of that carrier is stated rather than hidden: a data-string subject can silently stop compiling and still print a row, which is why the assertion on each leg is that the COMPILER produced a named diagnostic naming the parameter and the argument, and why the per-subject carriers are now authored in the sanctioned form: the refused subject lives INSIDE the leg as source text and is checked through the declared source-text door, never as a file the fold would have to swallow. The door for a class like this one is #dag.gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census::compile_dag_diagnostic_census (dag/gunbc/compile_diagnostic_census.dag), which typechecks a source string and hands back its rows; the parse-stage door conservation_subject_of_text cannot serve here, because it reaches LEX and NORMALIZE and stops, so it can observe no row for a typecheck-emitted refusal at any severity (src/v2/compiler/reference_conservation_admission.dag, `conservation_subject_of_text`). And the census door answers only on the ROUTE whose load leaves its closure authority uncontested -- the receipt below measures both refusals -- which is why the six wall legs and the seventeen witness legs are instrument legs under dag/gunbc/instruments/, not claims, executed by name one per dispatch with their own exit status: 0 held, 1 an observation that disagreed, 2 could not run with the door's cause named (#gunbc.compile_census_probe::census_exit). That double limit of the FORM -- the wrong door sees no row, the right door on the wrong route sees nothing -- is recorded here because the class needs it.",
    "THE DOOR'S ROUTE, MEASURED -- A LANE FACT, NOT A STYLE CHOICE. `compile_dag_diagnostic_census` is host-realized and builds a fixture closure over source roots; under the CLAIM route (`gunbc test`, the one claim entrypoint -- `gunbc run`'s own help refuses claims: 'Claims are not executed by this verb') it REFUSES, and there is exactly ONE cause on the record, because a cause is a fact only once it is PRINTED. An earlier draft of this row asserted a SECOND cause (`compile_dag_diagnostic_census: stdlib source is unresolved in this build`) and a 14-leg probe said which half of that string the door blamed; no log in stages3 carries that string -- grep for `stdlib source is unresolved`, for `CensusNotRunnable` and for `unresolved` returned 0 hits across every log then present -- and the property legs were computing verdicts over a string nothing printed. The sentence is therefore removed rather than repeated, and the legs were rewritten to PRINT what they test: each one hands the raw cause back as its own ExitFailure reason, which is how the harness renders it, so the claim line carries the verdict and the string it was computed from side by side -- <PLACEHOLDER-S100-CAUSE-LINES> -- on srv1, BOOT field `cut -c1-8 /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id` = c095c0cd, at head `e41d841e9e2871cdf0526637d0ca5491db19696c`. The SAME legs on the RUN route print `CAUSE[<the census ANSWERED on this route; no cause exists>]` with HELD=false, which is the whole route asymmetry in one field: the door ANSWERS on the run route and REFUSES on the claim route, so a property over a cause is only decidable where a cause exists. The single exact-label form over the three-root corpus (--source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2) is what refuses, with `SharedIndexSecondResidentPool: slot 0 already holds roots [\"dag\", \"src/v1\", \"src/v2\"]; roots [\"dag\", \"src/v2\"] demanded at src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs:3690 would be a second resident pool on this thread` -- the door demands its default pair while the claim route's own pool owns the slot. Consequence, stated so the next wall does not rediscover it: the claim route is ONE-SIDED on this witness, so it carries no discriminating pair. On the head tree at `9e5e8582f04e622bf8344f2ed2af1768b38f7632` it refuses every wall leg -- `UNOBSERVED outcome=ExitFailure code=2` with the pool cause in `detail=`, and its own status line `S94_REAL_EXIT|--wet=2` beside each: stages3/logs94_evidence.out lines 17, 24, 31, 38 are the legs and lines 19, 26, 33, 40 are those statuses. On the main carrier (main `6be13eea95b14c1735e3b096c086cc329866c92e`, binary `7d4edf2a6de0b7ff53444d84d62892f798cefafa627d66561a0348c4794e5425`) the same route EVALUATES them and prints the red half instead: `claim route: //test/claim/list_append_element_argument_wall/... -- 6 claim(s): 0 held, 6 did not hold, 0 unobserved` with `S92_REAL_EXIT|main_wet_wall_subtree=1`, and leg by leg at stages3/logs92_main.out lines 29, 36, 43, 51 (identically in logs90_main.out), every one rc=1. A route that answers red on one tree and cannot answer at all on the other is neither red nor green as a pair, which is why the legs are enrolled as instrument rows and the census lines below come from that route on both trees. Such legs were ejected from the batch and both modules moved out of `test.claim` entirely -- which also removes every fold claim the move would otherwise have enrolled into the corpus. THE INSTRUMENT ROUTE ANSWERS: `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --source-root src/v2 --entry <instrument> --function <leg>`, one leg per dispatch with its own rc line; the readings that differ between the two binaries on that route are the record, <PLACEHOLDER-LEG-TABLE-SENTENCE>",
    "ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed: of three candidate variants, only the seam-local selector refuses the repro; swapping the element read inside `run_element_demand` alone (V2) is measured irrelevant measured in stages3/logs42_runner.out, where the V2 patch is applied, built and reverted with its own exit statuses (S41_V2_APPLIED=1, S42_BUILD_V2_RC=0, binary S42_BIN_V2_SHA=1fded00a93ef8daa18ad666dbe7e6c70e7f9a8174b8428ac469fa38dc8b7636c, S42_LEGS_V2_RC=0, S42_REVERT_V2_RC=0), and under V2 the repro's own leg ACCEPTS it: S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_REAL_EXIT=0, S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_hard_lines=0, the runner's own label S42_v2S37_LEG_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER_VERDICT=AS-EXPECTED, and the global predicate (V3) is the refused one. The layer rule matters for any reader who re-runs this: the binary compiles the COMMITTED generated Rust, so a `.dag`-only edit is inert — the `.dag` half and the regenerated mirror half must BOTH land, and the mirror is emitter output (one heal round, `--required-regen --regen-emission-scope-carried --base-mirror --regen-affected-scope`, run twice with equal mirror sha e0e93afe46de7fd50b7cb2c97a491aca029b999be1eabbca83ddd532d4545438 on 2026-11-26, srv1 BOOT=c095c0cd, log stages3/logs45b_runner.out).",
    "WHICH ROUTE PRODUCED WHICH VERDICT FOR THIS ROW ITSELF, so a green never means more than it does: the derived-roster join claim `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` (src/v2/test/claim/derived_roster_seed_agreement.dag) EVALUATED `true` with this row present, and it did so by the RUN ROUTE (`gunbc run --entry <module> --function <name>`, head-built binary f2f660c147cb) -- so it is a run-route EVALUATION, not a PASS line; its rc 2 and its host complaint (`returned `true`, not `ProcessExit``) are the host mapping a verdict to an exit code, not a refusal by gunbc. The `gunbc test` route REFUSED both arms, with and without the row, at rc 2 (S52_REAL_EXIT|A_no_row=2, S52_REAL_EXIT|B_with_row=2), and the refusal text -- quoted verbatim from the per-leg logs, which is where it lives, not in the runner log -- is gunbc test: REFUSED cause=BinaryFreshnessUndecided — /home/briansrls/scratch/eager-heron-455/gunbc/target/release/gunbc: its dep-info names an input outside this worktree (/home/briansrls/scratch/eager-heron-455/gunbc); it was built from another checkout, so nothing here says whether it answers for this one Nothing on this row is claimed as a CI PASS line; the claim route over this row belongs to the staffing round, and the witness tier for this filing is parses + typechecks. Measured 2026-11-26 on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd, aarch64). THE FILES ARE NAMED AS THEY ARE, because the first filing named a set that did not contain two of these claims: the run-route evaluation line is S60C| error: function `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` returned `true`, not `ProcessExit`. in stages3/logs60_runner.out (and S59C| error: function `the_native_recurring_failure_mode_roster_agrees_with_the_seeds` returned `true`, not `ProcessExit`. in stages3/logs59_runner.out, the round that verified the committed bytes were the edited ones, S59_BLOB_IS_THE_EDITED_BYTES=yes); the test-route refusals are s52/A_no_row.log and s52/B_with_row.log with their exit statuses in stages3/logs52_runner.out (S52_REAL_EXIT|A_no_row=2, binary S52_BIN_SHA=f2f660c147cb42f610da3911cdfefb7ce7b9c3d8460ef3b6ab2c06c651c59ea0, tree S52_TREE_SHA=bc9f1a1b3e4730caf5e38da4c66eafa305b6780f).",
    "CARRIER OBLIGATION, TYPED RATHER THAN COMMENTED, BECAUSE THE ROW DEPENDS ON IT: the two positional fixtures named in the first filing are ABSENT from this repository and were never a committed carrier. `eh_f2_pair_same_container` and `eh_f2_repro_ticket` appear in no file name at any revision (S71_EH_F2_NAMES|ref=origin/main|count=0|rc=1, S71_EH_F2_NAMES|ref=885483f5e16c97a597c6d868164f03826cc3f1c9|count=0|rc=1, S71_EH_F2_NAMES|ref=892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16|count=0|rc=1), `git grep -l eh_f2_pair_same_container` is 0 at origin/main (S71_GREPL_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|ref=origin/main|count=0|rc=1), 0 at the implementation head (S71_GREPL_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|ref=892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16|count=0|rc=1), and 1 at this row's head (S71_GREPL_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|ref=885483f5e16c97a597c6d868164f03826cc3f1c9|count=1|rc=0) -- the single hit being this file naming them -- and `src/v1/test/claim/infer/`, where the first filing placed them, is not a path in the repository at all (S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=src/v1/test/claim|entries=0|rc=1, and S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=src/v1/test|entries=0|rc=1). What they were is recorded so the work is not repeated: scratch modules written at run time into `dag/test/claim/` by the stage-46 runner and deleted by that runner's own `trap cleanup EXIT`; they first ran on branch `session/eager-heron-455` at head 892a8ff9179b6f0a3afeecc654c4423365477a16 on srv1 (BOOT c095c0cd), in stages3/logs46b_runner.out, which does keep the obligation this row demands -- the subject's own compile exit status printed beside its census line: S46_LEGS|PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag|want=hard|REAL_EXIT=1|hard=2|arm=2|names_param_right=11, S46_LEGS|TICKET_REPRO|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_repro_ticket.dag|want=hard|REAL_EXIT=1|hard=2|arm=2|names_param_right=10, with the accepted controls S46_LEGS|TWO_LISTS|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_control_two_lists.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0 and S46_LEGS|LIST_PUSH|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_control_list_push.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0, and the same subjects accepted by main's RELEASED parser as they must be before the wall is credited: S46_LEGS|MAIN_RELEASED_PAIR_SAME_CONTAINER|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_pair_same_container.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0, S46_LEGS|MAIN_RELEASED_TICKET_REPRO|module=dag/test/claim/eh_f2_repro_ticket.dag|want=accept|REAL_EXIT=0|hard=0|arm=0|names_param_none=0. THE OBLIGATION IS DISCHARGED IN THE SANCTIONED FORM, NOT IN FILE FORM: the refused subjects are carried as source text INSIDE the instrument legs of dag/gunbc/instruments/list_append_element_argument_wall.dag (module gunbc.instruments.list_append_element_argument_wall), on one axis with only the swapped argument varying, fed through the declared source-text door #dag.gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census::compile_dag_diagnostic_census on the route where that door answers (the instrument route -- the claim-route refusal is measured in the receipt above), with each leg naming the census arm it matches (CensusObserved or CensusNotRunnable) and asserting the refusal's class, its parameter and its reason rather than a bare count, and with the two accepted arms required to be Runnable with zero blocking rows of the target class so an empty census cannot be confused with a census that did not run. No file was added to the fold and the known-red roster was not touched, which is the point of the form: a refused subject carried as text inside a claim cannot break the whole-tree fold, because it is never compiled as a module of the tree. The ABSENT findings above stay accurate for the two scratch files, which remain uncommitted. A file-form carrier is not owed; if a subject ever needs a multi-file tree that the source-text form cannot express, that is a finding about the FORM to be brought, not routed around by quietly adding a file. Counts are quoted from stages3/logs71_gitcounts.out, one command per line with its own exit status.",
    "STAGGER CHECK AT FILING, TYPED BECAUSE A SIBLING COLLISION DISSOLVES THIS FILING: `git grep -l` over origin/main and every open pull-request head for this row's stem and for its carrier module, hit counts in this PR's description. The swept paths carry their ground counts so a nil result has ground under it rather than being an empty grep: S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode|entries=1046|rc=0, S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=dag/test/claim|entries=2906|rc=0, S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=src/v2/test/claim|entries=1118|rc=0. `src/v1/test/claim`, swept by the first filing, is dropped from the list: S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=src/v1/test/claim|entries=0|rc=1 at origin/main -- a sweep over a path with no files returns nothing whatever a sibling did there, so it proves nothing and its silence must not be read as absence of collision. DISSOLUTION CONDITION: if another branch adds a row or a carrier naming this class, the two are joined before either is staffed; this row is FILED, not staffed. Counts quoted from stages3/logs71_gitcounts.out with each command's own exit status; origin/main at filing S71_ORIGIN_MAIN=27394a7718d8ab3b2f90e890a157a584984d244e.",
    "NODE PROVENANCE DEFERRED, TYPED BECAUSE THE ROW RELIES ON IT: this row states no roadmap_node identity and mints no `rn_`-prefixed value, because the `rn_` provenance rule is an OPEN operator question, not an answered one. `identity` is the file's own stem cast `as NonEmptyStr`, which is what the population does, measured rather than asserted: S72_POPULATION|rows=1046|identity_is_stem=1046|identity_other=0|identity_mints_rn=0|rc=0 -- every row's identity is its own stem and none mints an `rn_` value; the directory's entry count and its `.dag` count agree (S71_PATH_COUNT|ref=origin/main|path=dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode|entries=1046|rc=0 and S71_PATH_COUNT_DAG|ref=origin/main|path=dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode|entries=1046|rc=0), so no non-row file is being counted as a row. A withdrawn node identity is not carried here either; the two measured negatives in this row are its only record. DISSOLUTION CONDITION: staffing this row waits on the operator's ruling on `rn_` provenance and on the stagger check above; nothing here pretends either is settled. Counts quoted from stages3/logs72_identity.out and stages3/logs71_gitcounts.out with their exit statuses.",
    "THE WITNESS IS ENROLLED, AND REVIEW 99292 IS WHAT MOVED IT THERE. The first filing carried the witness at `dag/test/claim/text_at_free_monoid_run_carrier_witness.dag`, which is the path the roadmap node's red control names; the measured route facts in the note above moved both witness modules to `dag/gunbc/instruments/` as instrument legs, and review 99292 on gunb-ai/gunbc#16894 then found the moved modules DANGLING -- new, imported by nothing, no row in `gunbc.instrument_targets` -- against gunbc.design_argument::consumption ("a module nothing imports" is a listed tell), against the CI contract ("a `gunbc test <label>` address is a row in `gunbc.instrument_targets` bound through `gunbc.target_binding` `TargetProducer`"), and against the guarantee ladder's "the discriminating RED and positive control stay enrolled". Eleven rows now stand: six wall legs, three carrier legs, and one fold per module (six and seventeen legs) so no leg can exist unaddressed. They bind through `CliWireProgramProducer`, whose single host realization (src/v1/stage0/src/target_invocation_host.rs `run_cli_wire_program`) resolves the entry from the row's DECLARATION through gunbc.source_layout -- no authored path string to drift, the gunbc#8377 class -- evaluates the function wet over the witness layer roots, prints the wire bytes, and maps the leg's `ProcessExit` through the one classifier in cli_run; the legs answer a `CliWireResponse` through gunbc.compile_census_probe `census_leg_wire` / `census_legs_wire`, which hand the exit code through UNCHANGED because a mapper folding a door refusal (2) into a finding (1) would report a census that could not run as a wall that did not fire.",
    "A LABEL IS NOT RUNNABLE FROM A BINARY THAT DOES NOT KNOW IT, AND THAT IS A FACT ABOUT THIS REPOSITORY'S INSTRUMENT ROUTE WORTH RECORDING. The first run of the eleven labels answered status 2 for every one of them and printed the host's known-target population, which omitted all eleven: the host dispatches from `src/v1/stage0/src/instrument_registry_generated.rs`, which is EMITTED from `gunbc.instrument_targets` `instrument_bindings()` by #gunbc.instruments.instrument_registry_emit::instrument_registry_generated_text (the file's own header: "Generated by gunbc instruments.instrument_registry_emit -- do not hand-edit ... regenerate rather than edit"). So an instrument row and the regenerated registry land in the SAME commit -- a row without the regenerated file is an address that refuses, and the drift wall beside it (test.claim.instrument_registry_artifact_rendering_witness compares the committed bytes against the rendering) is what stops the two from separating again. Recording the failed attempt because the successful one looks like an ordinary label run and the order of operations is not guessable from either.",
    "THE ENROLLED ROUTE, EXECUTED, WITH THE RUNNER'S OWN EXIT BESIDE EVERY CENSUS LINE. Each instrument leg was dispatched on its label in ONE srv1 dispatch per leg, and the acquisition records the command and the runner's status verbatim -- `<identity>: HELD` or `<identity>: DID NOT HOLD rc=<code>: <door cause>` on one line, and `S99_REAL_EXIT|<tree>|gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:<label>=<rc>` on its own line beside it, so the reader sees the run happened instead of trusting this row's prose. <PLACEHOLDER-S99-TABLE> <PLACEHOLDER-RUN-LINK-S99>",
    "THE DIFFERENTIAL LEG WAS WRONG, AND ITS MEASUREMENT IS A FINDING ABOUT THE WALL, NOT ONLY ABOUT THE LEG. The leg `the_two_arms_differ_by_exactly_the_target_row` compared the refusing and admitting arms' FULL census histograms key by key, and it red. Measured at 95304b7f00c with this head's own binary (scratch module gunbc.instruments.eh_f2_arm_dump over the two fixtures, srv1 log stages3/logs96_armdump.out: BOOT field `cut -c1-8 /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id`), the arms differ at 25 keys and not one: 24 `EffectSummaryIncompleteAtFunctionValue` rows over std.algebra and std.list that the ADMITTING arm emits and the refusing arm does not -- once the call is refused, compilation stops lowering those sites, so those advisories are never produced -- plus one `TextRepresentationUnidentifiedAtBoundary` at `a call argument`, present only in the refusing arm at the refused actual. All 25 carry blocking=false, and every one is a CONSEQUENCE of the refusal rather than the refusal, so an advisory-inclusive differential reports this wall as under-observing the standard library. The leg now compares #gunbc.compile_diagnostic_census::census_blocking_rows keyed on the whole CensusKey (diagnostic_class, subject_name, blocking) with the exclusion and its measured reason written into the leg rather than performed. GENERALIZATION FOR THE CLASS: a located refusal changes the ADVISORY population of everything the compiled closure lowers, so any census differential taken across a refusing and an admitting arm must state which population it is about before it states its expectation.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
